{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he took.</b> Scripture says \"the wife of Moses\" and does not say \"his daughter,\" because Moses is more honored than her father's house:" "<b>After he sent her away.</b> Some say: after he gave her permission at the lodging-place to go to her father's house when he returned alone to the land of Egypt. And some say: after she sent gifts to him, like \"presents for his daughter\" (1 Kings 9:16)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:24.166642690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}